     {
      "id": "hs_kb01",
      "subject": "How to set up SAML SSO with Okta",
      "status": "active",
      "mailbox_id": "mb_general",
      "customer_email": "user1@customer.com",
      "tags": [
       "question"
      ],
      "threads": [
       {
        "id": "4175174435",
        "thread_type": "customer",
        "body": "How do I configure SAML SSO with Okta? I couldn't find any documentation.",
        "author_email": "user1@customer.com",
        "created_at": "2026-08-14T00:00:00"
       },
       {
        "id": "1335750708",
        "thread_type": "reply",
        "body": "Great question! Here's a step-by-step guide since we don't have this documented yet:\n\n1. Go to Okta Admin > Applications > Add Application\n2. Select 'SAML 2.0' as the sign-on method\n3. Set the Single Sign-On URL to https://app.example.com/sso/callback\n4. Set the Audience URI to https://app.example.com\n5. Under Attribute Statements, add: email -> user.email, name -> user.displayName\n6. Download the metadata XML\n7. In our app, go to Settings > Security > SSO and upload the metadata\n\nWe should really add this to our docs.",
        "author_email": "agent@support.com",
        "created_at": "2026-08-14T00:00:00"
       }
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-08-14T00:00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-14T00:00:00"
     },
     {
      "id": "hs_kb02",
      "subject": "API v2 docs show wrong endpoint",
      "status": "active",
      "mailbox_id": "mb_general",
      "customer_email": "dev@partner.io",
      "tags": [
       "bug-report"
      ],
      "threads": [
       {
        "id": "1017829115",
        "thread_type": "customer",
        "body": "The docs at docs.example.com/api/v2/users say to use POST /api/v2/users/create but that endpoint returns 404. The actual endpoint is POST /api/v2/users.",
        "author_email": "dev@partner.io",
        "created_at": "2026-08-14T00:00:00"
       },
       {
        "id": "2434204566",
        "thread_type": "reply",
        "body": "You're absolutely right - the documentation is outdated. The correct endpoint is POST /api/v2/users. We changed this in v2.3 but the docs weren't updated.",
        "author_email": "agent@support.com",
        "created_at": "2026-08-14T00:00:00"
       }
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-08-14T00:00:00",
